  "step_3": "The decision reason requires computing an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes and then evaluating which lottery has a higher chance of exceeding this level (i.e., positive differences). The aspiration level (-2333.33) and the resulting positive deviation only in Lottery A (20% chance of 0 Euros) are not reflected in the verbal report. The individual does not reference any such reference point or perform calculations involving averaging outcomes or comparing deviations from a central value. Instead, the justification is based on risk perception, loss avoidance, and a comparison of certainty versus uncertainty of loss. The reasoning in the report is consistent with a risk-aversion or minimax-type heuristic, not the aspiration-level rule described. There is no alignment between the information used in the reason (mean of outcomes, deviations) and that used by the individual (probability of avoiding loss, perceived increase in risk). Similarly, the justification (B is more attractive due to lower risk) contradicts the preference implied by the decision reason (which would favor A due to a chance of positive deviation). Therefore, there is no evidence the individual used this decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

